cally through the<!-- --> <a class="text-foreground underline underline-offset-2 decoration-current/40 hover:text-accent-foreground hover:decoration-current transition-colors text-xs cursor-pointer" href="/docs/api/api-reference/endpoints/list-endpoints">Endpoints API</a>. <a class="text-foreground underline underline-offset-2 decoration-current/40 hover:text-accent-foreground hover:decoration-current transition-colors text-xs cursor-pointer" href="/docs/provider-routing">Learn more</a> about our load balancing and customization options.</p></div></div></div><script>$RC("B:7","S:7")</script><div hidden id="S:8"><div class="flex w-full flex-col"><div class="mx-auto w-full flex flex-col gap-8 lg:flex-row lg:gap-16"><div class="flex flex-col gap-5 lg:w-1/2 lg:justify-between lg:gap-0"><div class="grid w-full grid-cols-12 items-center"><div class="col-span-1 text-left text-muted-foreground">1<!-- -->.</div><div class="col-span-7 flex min-w-0 items-center gap-4 text-left"><div class="relative flex items-center justify-center box-content p-px overflow-hidden rounded-sm bg-background size-6 shrink-0"><div class="absolute inset-px flex items-center justify-center [&amp;_img]:absolute [&amp;_img]:inset-0 [&amp;_img]:size-full [&amp;_img]:object-contain [&amp;_img]:rounded-sm"><div class="size-full"><picture class="h-full w-full shrink-0"><img width="256" height="256" alt="Favicon for https://claude.ai/apple-touch-icon.png" class="h-full w-full object-cover" src="/api/frontend/v1/image-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Fclaude.ai%2Fapple-touch-icon.png" loading="lazy" decoding="async"/></picture></div></div><div aria-hidden="true" class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-0 rounded-[inherit] ring-1 ring-inset ring-border/60 dark:inset-px dark:ring-white"></div></div><div class="flex min-w-0 flex-col"><a class="text-foreground underline underline-offset-2 decoration-current/40 hover:text-accent-foreground hover:decoration-current transition-colors cursor-pointer group text-xs block truncate font-medium" href="/apps/claude-code">Claude Code<!-- --> <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true" data-slot="icon" class="inline w-4 transition-transform group-hover:translate-x-0.5"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M16.28 11.47a.75.75 0 0 1 0 1.06l-7.5 7.5a.75.75 0 0 1-1.06-1.06L14.69 12 7.72 5.03a.75.75 0 0 1 1.06-1.06l7.5 7.5Z" clip-rule="evenodd"></path></svg></a><div class="text-muted-foreground flex items-center gap-1 text-xs"><span class="truncate cursor-help inline-block" role="button" tabindex="0" data-base-ui-click-trigger="" id="base-ui-_R_dl2rpepbqubsnqbt3dml9ivb_">Claude Code is Anthropic&#x27;s agentic coding tool that reads your entire codebase, plans and executes changes across files, runs tests, and iterates on failures, all from natural language prompts.</span></div></div></div><div class="col-span-4 flex items-center justify-end gap-3 text-right text-muted-foreground text-xs"><div><span>809B</span><span class="ml-1">tokens</span></div></div></div><div class="grid w-full grid-cols-12 items-center"><div class="col-span-1 text-left text-muted-foreground">2<!-- -->.</div><div class="col-span-7 flex min-w-0 items-center gap-4 text-left"><div class="relative flex items-center justify-center box-content p-px overflow-hidden rounded-sm bg-background size-6 shrink-0"><div class="absolute inset-px flex items-center justify-center [&amp;_img]:absolute [&amp;_img]:inset-0 [&amp;_img]:size-full [&amp;_img]:object-contain [&amp;_img]:rounded-sm"><div class="size-full"><picture class="h-full w-full shrink-0"><img width="256" height="256" alt="Favicon for https://nousresearch.com" class="h-full w-full object-cover" src="https://t0.gstatic.com/faviconV2?client=SOCIAL&amp;type=FAVICON&amp;fallback_opts=TYPE,SIZE,URL&amp;url=https://nousresearch.com&amp;size=256" loading="lazy" decoding="async"/></picture></div></div><div aria-hidden="true" class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-0 rounded-[inherit] ring-1 ring-inset ring-border/60 dark:inset-px dark:ring-white"></div></div><div class="flex min-w-0 flex-col"><a class="text-foreground underline underline-offset-2 decoration-current/40 hover:text-accent-foreground hover:decoration-current transition-colors cursor-pointer group text-xs block truncate font-medium" href="/apps/hermes-agent">Hermes Agent<!-- --> <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true" data-slot="icon" class="inline w-4 transition-transform group-hover:translate-x-0.5"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M16.28 11.47a.75.75 0 0 1 0 1.06l-7.5 7.5a.75.75 0 0 1-1.06-1.06L14.69 12 7.72 5.03a.75.75 0 0 1 1.06-1.06l7.5 7.5Z" clip-rule="evenodd"></path></svg></a><div class="text-muted-foreground flex items-center gap-1 text-xs"><span class="truncate cursor-help inline-block" role="button" tabindex="0" data-base-ui-click-trigger="" id="base-ui-_R_dl4rpepbqubsnqbt3dml9ivb_">Hermes Agent is an open-source, self-improving AI agent by Nous Research that runs persistently with memory across sessions, and builds reusable skills from experience. It comes with 40+ built-in tools, including web search, browser automation, and vision, plus scheduled automations and subagents.</span></div></div></div><div class="col-span-4 flex items-center justify-end gap-3 text-right text-muted-foreground text-xs"><div><span>688B</span><span class="ml-1">tokens</span></div></div></div><div class="grid w-full grid-cols-12 items-center"><div class="col-span-1 text-left text-muted-foreground">3<!-- -->.</div><div class="col-span-7 flex min-w-0 items-center gap-4 text-left"><div class="relative flex items-center justify-center box-content p-px overflow-hidden rounded-sm bg-background size-6 shrink-0"><div class="absolute inset-px flex items-center justify-center [&amp;_img]:absolute [&amp;_img]:inset-0 [&amp;_img]:size-full [&amp;_img]:object-contain [&amp;_img]:rounded-sm"><div class="size-full"><picture class="h-full w-full shrink-0"><img width="256" height="256" alt="Favicon for https://descript.com/" class="h-full w-full object-cover" src="https://t0.gstatic.com/faviconV2?client=SOCIAL&amp;type=FAVICON&amp;fallback_opts=TYPE,SIZE,URL&amp;url=https://descript.com/&amp;size=256" loading="lazy" decoding="async"/></picture></div></div><div aria-hidden="true" class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-0 rounded-[inherit] ring-1 ring-inset ring-border/60 dark:inset-px dark:ring-white"></div></div><div class="flex min-w-0 flex-col"><a class="text-foreground underline underline-offset-2 decoration-current/40 hover:text-accent-foreground hover:decoration-current transition-colors cursor-pointer group text-xs block truncate font-medium" href="/apps/descript">Descript<!-- --> <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true" data-slot="icon" class="inline w-4 transition-transform group-hover:translate-x-0.5"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M16.28 11.47a.75.75 0 0 1 0 1.06l-7.5 7.5a.75.75 0 0 1-1.06-1.06L14.69 12 7.72 5.03a.75.75 0 0 1 1.06-1.06l7.5 7.5Z" clip-rule="evenodd"></path></svg></a><div class="text-muted-foreground flex items-center gap-1 text-xs"><span class="truncate cursor-help inline-block" role="button" tabindex="0" data-base-ui-click-trigger="" id="base-ui-_R_dl6rpepbqubsnqbt3dml9ivb_">AI Video &amp; Podcast Editor</span></div></div></div><div class="col-span-4 flex items-center justify-end gap-3 text-right text-muted-foreground text-xs"><div><span>555B</span><span class="ml-1">tokens</span></div></div></div><div class="grid w-full grid-cols-12 items-center"><div class="col-span-1 text-left text-muted-foreground">4<!-- -->.</div><div class="col-span-7 flex min-w-0 items-center gap-4 text-left"><div class="relative flex items-center justify-center box-content p-px overflow-hidden rounded-sm bg-background size-6 shrink-0"><div class="absolute inset-px flex items-center justify-center [&amp;_img]:absolute [&amp;_img]:inset-0 [&amp;_img]:size-full [&amp;_img]:object-contain [&amp;_img]:rounded-sm"><div class="size-full"><picture class="h-full w-full shrink-0"><img width="256" height="256" alt="Favicon for https://hellohaven.ai/" class="h-full w-full object-cover" src="https://t0.gstatic.com/faviconV2?client=SOCIAL&amp;type=FAVICON&amp;fallback_opts=TYPE,SIZE,URL&amp;url=https://hellohaven.ai/&amp;size=256" loading="lazy" decoding="async"/></picture></div></div><div aria-hidden="true" class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-0 rounded-[inherit] ring-1 ring-inset ring-border/60 dark:inset-px dark:ring-white"></div></div><div class="flex min-w-0 flex-col"><a class="text-foreground underline underline-offset-2 decoration-current/40 hover:text-accent-foreground hover:decoration-current transition-colors cursor-pointer group text-xs block truncate font-medium" href="/apps/url/https%3A%2F%2Fhellohaven.ai%2F">Haven Talk Blue Sandbox<!-- --> <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true" data-slot="icon" class="inline w-4 transition-transform group-hover:translate-x-0.5"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M16.28 11.47a.75.75 0 0 1 0 1.06l-7.5 7.5a.75.75 0 0 1-1.06-1.06L14.69 12 7.72 5.03a.75.75 0 0 1 1.06-1.06l7.5 7.5Z" clip-rule="evenodd"></path></svg></a><div class="text-muted-foreground flex items-center gap-1 text-xs"><span class="text-faint">new</span></div></div></div><div class="col-span-4 flex items-center justify-end gap-3 text-right text-muted-foreground text-xs"><div><span>123B</span><span class="ml-1">tokens</span></div></div></div><div class="grid w-full grid-cols-12 items-center"><div class="col-span-1 text-left text-muted-foreground">5<!-- -->.</div><div class="col-span-7 flex min-w-0 items-center gap-4 text-left"><div class="relative flex items-center justify-center box-content p-px overflow-hidden rounded-sm bg-background size-6 shrink-0"><div class="absolute inset-px flex items-center justify-center [&amp;_img]:absolute [&amp;_img]:inset-0 [&amp;_img]:size-full [&amp;_img]:object-contain [&amp;_img]:rounded-sm"><div class="size-full"><picture class="h-full w-full shrink-0"><img width="256" height="256" alt="Favicon for https://openclaw.ai/" class="h-full w-full object-cover" src="https://t0.gstatic.com/faviconV2?client=SOCIAL&amp;type=FAVICON&amp;fallback_opts=TYPE,SIZE,URL&amp;url=https://openclaw.ai/&amp;size=256" loading="lazy" decoding="async"/></picture></div></div><div aria-hidden="true" class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-0 rounded-[inherit] ring-1 ring-inset ring-border/60 dark:inset-px dark:ring-white"></div></div><div class="flex min-w-0 flex-col"><a class="text-foreground underline underline-offset-2 decoration-current/40 hover:text-accent-foreground hover:decoration-current transition-colors cursor-pointer group text-xs block truncate font-medium" href="/apps/openclaw">OpenClaw<!-- --> <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true" data-slot="icon" class="inline w-4 transition-transform group-hover:translate-x-0.5"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M16.28 11.47a.75.75 0 0 1 0 1.06l-7.5 7.5a.75.75 0 0 1-1.06-1.06L14.69 12 7.72 5.03a.75.75 0 0 1 1.06-1.06l7.5 7.5Z" clip-rule="evenodd"></path></svg></a><div class="text-muted-foreground flex items-center gap-1 text-xs"><span class="truncate cursor-help inline-block" role="button" tabindex="0" data-base-ui-click-trigger="" id="base-ui-_R_dlarpepbqubsnqbt3dml9ivb_">OpenClaw is an open-source AI agent that connects to your messaging apps and takes real actions on your behalf, from running commands and browsing the web to managing files and sending emails.</span></div></div></div><div class="col-span-4 flex items-center justify-end gap-3 text-right text-muted-foreground text-xs"><div><span>98.4B</span><span class="ml-1">tokens</span></div></div></div></div><div class="lg:w-1/2"><div class="recharts-responsive-container relative z-10 w-full [&amp;_svg]:outline-hidden" style="width:100%;height:320px;min-width:0"><div style="width:0;overflow-x:visible"></div></div></div></div></div></div><script>$RC("B:8","S:8")</script><div hidden id="S:9"><section id="faq" class="scroll-mt-[calc(var(--navbar-height)+129px+var(--sticky-banner-top,0px))] lg:scroll-mt-[calc(var(--navbar-height)+70px+var(--sticky-banner-top,0px))] mb-10 last:mb-0"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-4 gap-y-2 mb-3"><div class="flex min-w-0 items-center gap-2"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-circle-question-mark h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-muted-foreground" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle><path d="M9.09 9a3 3 0 0 1 5.83 1c0 2-3 3-3 3"></path><path d="M12 17h.01"></path></svg><h2 class="text-base font-medium">Frequently asked questions</h2></div></div><div class="rounded-lg border border-border border-none p-0"><div class="overflow-hidden rounded-lg border border-border bg-card text-card-foreground px-4" data-orientation="vertical" dir="ltr" role="region"><div data-orientation="vertical" data-index="-1" data-closed="" class="border-b border-border last:border-0"><h3 data-orientation="vertical" data-index="-1" data-closed="" class="flex"><button type="button" data-value="" data-orientation="vertical" data-index="-1" aria-disabled="false" aria-expanded="false" id="base-ui-_R_taepbqubsnqbt3dml9ivbH2_" tabindex="0" class="flex flex-1 cursor-pointer items-center justify-between font-medium transition-colors duration-fast ease-smooth-out focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:border-focus-border focus-visible:shadow-focus [&amp;[data-panel-open]&gt;svg.accordion-chevron]:-scale-y-100 gap-4 py-4 text-left text-base hover:text-foreground">What is Claude Sonnet 5?<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down accordion-chevron size-4 shrink-0 text-muted-foreground transition-transform duration-fast ease-smooth-out motion-reduce:transition-none [&amp;_path]:[vector-effect:non-scaling-stroke]" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></button></h3><div data-orientation="vertical" data-index="-1" data-closed="" hidden="" id="base-ui-_R_taepbqubsnqbt3dml9ivbH1_" aria-labelledby="base-ui-_R_taepbqubsnqbt3dml9ivbH2_" role="region" style="--accordion-panel-height:auto;--accordion-panel-width:auto" data-testid="faq-panel" class="h-(--accordion-panel-height) overflow-hidden transition-[height,opacity] duration-slow ease-smooth-out data-[starting-style]:h-0 data-[starting-style]:opacity-0 data-[ending-style]:h-0 data-[ending-style]:opacity-0 data-[ending-style]:duration-medium motion-reduce:transition-opacity motion-reduce:duration-quick motion-reduce:data-[ending-style]:duration-quick motion-reduce:data-[starting-style]:h-auto motion-reduce:data-[ending-style]:h-auto text-body leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground [&amp;&gt;div]:pb-4"><div class="pb-3 pt-0"><p class="mb-3 whitespace-pre-wrap break-words leading-6 last:mb-0">Sonnet 5 is Anthropic&#x27;s most capable Sonnet-class model, with frontier performance across coding, agents, and professional work. It supports adaptive thinking with selectable reasoning effort levels (low, medium, high, max, and x-high), a 1M-token context window, and text, image, and file inputs.</p></div></div></div><div data-orientation="vertical" data-index="-1" data-closed="" class="border-b border-border last:border-0"><h3 data-orientation="vertical" data-index="-1" data-closed="" class="flex"><button type="button" data-value="" data-orientation="vertical" data-index="-1" aria-disabled="false" aria-expanded="false" id="base-ui-_R_1daepbqubsnqbt3dml9ivbH2_" tabindex="0" class="flex flex-1 cursor-pointer items-center justify-between font-medium transition-colors duration-fast ease-smooth-out focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:border-focus-border focus-visible:shadow-focus [&amp;[data-panel-open]&gt;svg.accordion-chevron]:-scale-y-100 gap-4 py-4 text-left text-base hover:text-foreground">Where is the Claude Sonnet 5 documentation?<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down accordion-chevron size-4 shrink-0 text-muted-foreground transition-transform duration-fast ease-smooth-out motion-reduce:transition-none [&amp;_path]:[vector-effect:non-scaling-stroke]" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></button></h3><div data-orientation="vertical" data-index="-1" data-closed="" hidden="" id="base-ui-_R_1daepbqubsnqbt3dml9ivbH1_" aria-labelledby="base-ui-_R_1daepbqubsnqbt3dml9ivbH2_" role="region" style="--accordion-panel-height:auto;--accordion-panel-width:auto" data-testid="faq-panel" class="h-(--accordion-panel-height) overflow-hidden transition-[height,opacity] duration-slow ease-smooth-out data-[starting-style]:h-0 data-[starting-style]:opacity-0 data-[ending-style]:h-0 data-[ending-style]:opacity-0 data-[ending-style]:duration-medium motion-reduce:transition-opacity motion-reduce:duration-quick motion-reduce:data-[ending-style]:duration-quick motion-reduce:data-[starting-style]:h-auto motion-reduce:data-[ending-style]:h-auto text-body leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground [&amp;&gt;div]:pb-4"><div class="pb-3 pt-0"><p class="mb-3 whitespace-pre-wrap break-words leading-6 last:mb-0">The Claude Sonnet 5 documentation on OpenRouter includes the <a href="/docs/cookbook/evaluate-and-optimize/model-migrations/sonnet-5" class="underline underline-offset-2 decoration-current/40 hover:text-accent-foreground hover:decoration-current transition-colors">Claude 5 Sonnet Migration Guide</a> cookbook. The <a href="/docs/quickstart" class="underline underline-offset-2 decoration-current/40 hover:text-accent-foreground hover:decoration-current transition-colors">quickstart</a> covers API keys and your first request, and the <a href="/docs/api-reference/overview" class="underline underline-offset-2 decoration-current/40 hover:text-accent-foreground hover:decoration-current transition-colors">API reference</a> lists every parameter.</p></div></div></div><div data-orientation="vertical" data-index="-1" data-closed="" class="border-b border-border last:border-0"><h3 data-orientation="vertical" data-index="-1" data-closed="" class="flex"><button type="button" data-value="" data-orientation="vertical" data-index="-1" aria-disabled="false" aria-expanded="false" id="base-ui-_R_1taepbqubsnqbt3dml9ivbH2_" tabindex="0" class="flex flex-1 cursor-pointer items-center justify-between font-medium transition-colors duration-fast ease-smooth-out focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:border-focus-border focus-visible:shadow-focus [&amp;[data-panel-open]&gt;svg.accordion-chevron]:-scale-y-100 gap-4 py-4 text-left text-base hover:text-foreground">How much does Claude Sonnet 5 cost?<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down accordion-chevron size-4 shrink-0 text-muted-foreground transition-transform duration-fast ease-smooth-out motion-reduce:transition-none [&amp;_path]:[vector-effect:non-scaling-stroke]" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></button></h3><div data-orientation="vertical" data-index="-1" data-closed="" hidden="" id="base-ui-_R_1taepbqubsnqbt3dml9ivbH1_" aria-labelledby="base-ui-_R_1taepbqubsnqbt3dml9ivbH2_" role="region" style="--accordion-panel-height:auto;--accordion-panel-width:auto" data-testid="faq-panel" class="h-(--accordion-panel-height) overflow-hidden transition-[height,opacity] duration-slow ease-smooth-out data-[starting-style]:h-0 data-[starting-style]:opacity-0 data-[ending-style]:h-0 data-[ending-style]:opacity-0 data-[ending-style]:duration-medium motion-reduce:transition-opacity motion-reduce:duration-quick motion-reduce:data-[ending-style]:duration-quick motion-reduce:data-[starting-style]:h-auto motion-reduce:data-[ending-style]:h-auto text-body leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground [&amp;&gt;div]:pb-4"><div class="pb-3 pt-0"><p class="mb-3 whitespace-pre-wrap break-words leading-6 last:mb-0">Claude Sonnet 5 costs $2.00/M input tokens and $10.00/M output tokens, with separate rates for Cache Read at $0.20/M tokens, Cache Write at $2.50/M tokens, Cache Write (1h) at $4.00/M tokens, and Web Search at $10.00/1K calls.</p></div></div></div><div data-orientation="vertical" data-index="-1" data-closed="" class="border-b border-border last:border-0"><h3 data-orientation="vertical" data-index="-1" data-closed="" class="flex"><button type="button" data-value="" data-orientation="vertical" data-index="-1" aria-disabled="false" aria-expanded="false" id="base-ui-_R_2daepbqubsnqbt3dml9ivbH2_" tabindex="0" class="flex flex-1 cursor-pointer items-center justify-between font-medium transition-colors duration-fast ease-smooth-out focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:border-focus-border focus-visible:shadow-focus [&amp;[data-panel-open]&gt;svg.accordion-chevron]:-scale-y-100 gap-4 py-4 text-left text-base hover:text-foreground">What is the context length of Claude Sonnet 5?<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down accordion-chevron size-4 shrink-0 text-muted-foreground transition-transform duration-fast ease-smooth-out motion-reduce:transition-none [&amp;_path]:[vector-effect:non-scaling-stroke]" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></button></h3><div data-orientation="vertical" data-index="-1" data-closed="" hidden="" id="base-ui-_R_2daepbqubsnqbt3dml9ivbH1_" aria-labelledby="base-ui-_R_2daepbqubsnqbt3dml9ivbH2_" role="region" style="--accordion-panel-height:auto;--accordion-panel-width:auto" data-testid="faq-panel" class="h-(--accordion-panel-height) overflow-hidden transition-[height,opacity] duration-slow ease-smooth-out data-[starting-style]:h-0 data-[starting-style]:opacity-0 data-[ending-style]:h-0 data-[ending-style]:opacity-0 data-[ending-style]:duration-medium motion-reduce:transition-opacity motion-reduce:duration-quick motion-reduce:data-[ending-style]:duration-quick motion-reduce:data-[starting-style]:h-auto motion-reduce:data-[ending-style]:h-auto text-body leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground [&amp;&gt;div]:pb-4"><div class="pb-3 pt-0"><p class="mb-3 whitespace-pre-wrap break-words leading-6 last:mb-0">Claude Sonnet 5 has a 1,000,000 token context window. It supports up to 128,000 completion tokens.</p></div></div></div><div data-orientation="vertical" data-index="-1" data-closed="" class="border-b border-border last:border-0"><h3 data-orientation="vertical" data-index="-1" data-closed="" class="flex"><button type="button" data-value="" data-orientation="vertical" data-index="-1" aria-disabled="false" aria-expanded="false" id="base-ui-_R_2taepbqubsnqbt3dml9ivbH2_" tabindex="0" class="flex flex-1 cursor-pointer items-center justify-between font-medium transition-colors duration-fast ease-smooth-out focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:border-focus-border focus-visible:shadow-focus [&amp;[data-panel-open]&gt;svg.accordion-chevron]:-scale-y-100 gap-4 py-4 text-left text-base hover:text-foreground">Does Claude Sonnet 5 support tool calling and structured outputs?<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down accordion-chevron size-4 shrink-0 text-muted-foreground transition-transform duration-fast ease-smooth-out motion-reduce:transition-none [&amp;_path]:[vector-effect:non-scaling-stroke]" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></button></h3><div data-orientation="vertical" data-index="-1" data-closed="" hidden="" id="base-ui-_R_2taepbqubsnqbt3dml9ivbH1_" aria-labelledby="base-ui-_R_2taepbqubsnqbt3dml9ivbH2_" role="region" style="--accordion-panel-height:auto;--accordion-panel-width:auto" data-testid="faq-panel" class="h-(--accordion-panel-height) overflow-hidden transition-[height,opacity] duration-slow ease-smooth-out data-[starting-style]:h-0 data-[starting-style]:opacity-0 data-[ending-style]:h-0 data-[ending-style]:opacity-0 data-[ending-style]:duration-medium motion-reduce:transition-opacity motion-reduce:duration-quick motion-reduce:data-[ending-style]:duration-quick motion-reduce:data-[starting-style]:h-auto motion-reduce:data-[ending-style]:h-auto text-body leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground [&amp;&gt;div]:pb-4"><div class="pb-3 pt-0"><p class="mb-3 whitespace-pre-wrap break-words leading-6 last:mb-0">Yes. Claude Sonnet 5 accepts <code class="rounded-md bg-card-hover px-1.5 text-foreground">tools</code> and <code class="rounded-md bg-card-hover px-1.5 text-foreground">tool_choice</code> for function calling. It also supports structured outputs via a JSON schema in <code class="rounded-md bg-card-hover px-1.5 text-foreground">response_format</code>.</p></div></div></div><div data-orientation="vertical" data-index="-1" data-closed="" class="border-b border-border last:border-0"><h3 data-orientation="vertical" data-index="-1" data-closed="" class="flex"><button type="button" data-value="" data-orientation="vertical" data-index="-1" aria-disabled="false" aria-expanded="false" id="base-ui-_R_3daepbqubsnqbt3dml9ivbH2_" tabindex="0" class="flex flex-1 cursor-pointer items-center justify-between font-medium transition-colors duration-fast ease-smooth-out focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:border-focus-border focus-visible:shadow-focus [&amp;[data-panel-open]&gt;svg.accordion-chevron]:-scale-y-100 gap-4 py-4 text-left text-base hover:text-foreground">What inputs and outputs does Claude Sonnet 5 support?<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down accordion-chevron size-4 shrink-0 text-muted-foreground transition-transform duration-fast ease-smooth-out motion-reduce:transition-none [&amp;_path]:[vector-effect:non-scaling-stroke]" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></button></h3><div data-orientation="vertical" data-index="-1" data-closed="" hidden="" id="base-ui-_R_3daepbqubsnqbt3dml9ivbH1_" aria-labelledby="base-ui-_R_3daepbqubsnqbt3dml9ivbH2_" role="region" style="--accordion-panel-height:auto;--accordion-panel-width:auto" data-testid="faq-panel" class="h-(--accordion-panel-height) overflow-hidden transition-[height,opacity] duration-slow ease-smooth-out data-[starting-style]:h-0 data-[starting-style]:opacity-0 data-[ending-style]:h-0 data-[ending-style]:opacity-0 data-[ending-style]:duration-medium motion-reduce:transition-opacity motion-reduce:duration-quick motion-reduce:data-[ending-style]:duration-quick motion-reduce:data-[starting-style]:h-auto motion-reduce:data-[ending-style]:h-auto text-body leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground [&amp;&gt;div]:pb-4"><div class="pb-3 pt-0"><p class="mb-3 whitespace-pre-wrap break-words leading-6 last:mb-0">Claude Sonnet 5 accepts text, images, and files such as PDFs as input and returns text.</p></div></div></div><div data-orientation="vertical" data-index="-1" data-closed="" class="border-b border-border last:border-0"><h3 data-orientation="vertical" data-index="-1" data-closed="" class="flex"><button type="button" data-value="" data-orientation="vertical" data-index="-1" aria-disabled="false" aria-expanded="false" id="base-ui-_R_3taepbqubsnqbt3dml9ivbH2_" tabindex="0" class="flex flex-1 cursor-pointer items-center justify-between font-medium transition-colors duration-fast ease-smooth-out focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:border-focus-border focus-visible:shadow-focus [&amp;[data-panel-open]&gt;svg.accordion-chevron]:-scale-y-100 gap-4 py-4 text-left text-base hover:text-foreground">Which providers serve Claude Sonnet 5?<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down accordion-chevron size-4 shrink-0 text-muted-foreground transition-transform duration-fast ease-smooth-out motion-reduce:transition-none [&amp;_path]:[vector-effect:non-scaling-stroke]" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></button></h3><div data-orientation="vertical" data-index="-1" data-closed="" hidden="" id="base-ui-_R_3taepbqubsnqbt3dml9ivbH1_" aria-labelledby="base-ui-_R_3taepbqubsnqbt3dml9ivbH2_" role="region" style="--accordion-panel-height:auto;--accordion-panel-width:auto" data-testid="faq-panel" class="h-(--accordion-panel-height) overflow-hidden transition-[height,opacity] duration-slow ease-smooth-out data-[starting-style]:h-0 data-[starting-style]:opacity-0 data-[ending-style]:h-0 data-[ending-style]:opacity-0 data-[ending-style]:duration-medium motion-reduce:transition-opacity motion-reduce:duration-quick motion-reduce:data-[ending-style]:duration-quick motion-reduce:data-[starting-style]:h-auto motion-reduce:data-[ending-style]:h-auto text-body leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground [&amp;&gt;div]:pb-4"><div class="pb-3 pt-0"><p class="mb-3 whitespace-pre-wrap break-words leading-6 last:mb-0">Claude Sonnet 5 is served by 5 providers on OpenRouter: Claude Platform on AWS, Azure, Google Vertex, Amazon Bedrock, and Anthropic. Requests are routed to the best available provider, with automatic failover to the others, and you can pin or exclude providers with <a href="/docs/features/provider-routing" class="underline underline-offset-2 decoration-current/40 hover:text-accent-foreground hover:decoration-current transition-colors">provider routing</a>.</p></div></div></div><div data-orientation="vertical" data-index="-1" data-closed="" class="border-b border-border last:border-0"><h3 data-orientation="vertical" data-index="-1" data-closed="" class="flex"><button type="button" data-value="" data-orientation="vertical" data-index="-1" aria-disabled="false" aria-expanded="false" id="base-ui-_R_4daepbqubsnqbt3dml9ivbH2_" tabindex="0" class="flex flex-1 cursor-pointer items-center justify-between font-medium transition-colors duration-fast ease-smooth-out focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:border-focus-border focus-visible:shadow-focus [&amp;[data-panel-open]&gt;svg.accordion-chevron]:-scale-y-100 gap-4 py-4 text-left text-base hover:text-foreground">When was Claude Sonnet 5 released?<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down accordion-chevron size-4 shrink-0 text-muted-foreground transition-transform duration-fast ease-smooth-out motion-reduce:transition-none [&amp;_path]:[vector-effect:non-scaling-stroke]" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></button></h3><div data-orientation="vertical" data-index="-1" data-closed="" hidden="" id="base-ui-_R_4daepbqubsnqbt3dml9ivbH1_" aria-labelledby="base-ui-_R_4daepbqubsnqbt3dml9ivbH2_" role="region" style="--accordion-panel-height:auto;--accordion-panel-width:auto" data-testid="faq-panel" class="h-(--accordion-panel-height) overflow-hidden transition-[height,opacity] duration-slow ease-smooth-out data-[starting-style]:h-0 data-[starting-style]:opacity-0 data-[ending-style]:h-0 data-[ending-style]:opacity-0 data-[ending-style]:duration-medium motion-reduce:transition-opacity motion-reduce:duration-quick motion-reduce:data-[ending-style]:duration-quick motion-reduce:data-[starting-style]:h-auto motion-reduce:data-[ending-style]:h-auto text-body leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground [&amp;&gt;div]:pb-4"><div class="pb-3 pt-0"><p class="mb-3 whitespace-pre-wrap break-words leading-6 last:mb-0">Claude Sonnet 5 was released on June 30, 2026.</p></div></div></div></div></div></section><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What is Claude Sonnet 5?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Sonnet 5 is Anthropic's most capable Sonnet-class model, with frontier performance across coding, agents, and professional work. It supports adaptive thinking with selectable reasoning effort levels (low, medium, high, max, and x-high), a 1M-token context window, and text, image, and file inputs."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Where is the Claude Sonnet 5 documentation?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The Claude Sonnet 5 documentation on OpenRouter includes the Claude 5 Sonnet Migration Guide cookbook. The quickstart covers API keys and your first request, and the API reference lists every parameter."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much does Claude Sonnet 5 cost?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Claude Sonnet 5 costs $2.00/M input tokens and $10.00/M output tokens, with separate rates for Cache Read at $0.20/M tokens, Cache Write at $2.50/M tokens, Cache Write (1h) at $4.00/M tokens, and Web Search at $10.00/1K calls."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the context length of Claude Sonnet 5?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Claude Sonnet 5 has a 1,000,000 token context window. It supports up to 128,000 completion tokens."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does Claude Sonnet 5 support tool calling and structured outputs?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Claude Sonnet 5 accepts tools and tool_choice for function calling. It also supports structured outputs via a JSON schema in response_format."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What inputs and outputs does Claude Sonnet 5 support?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Claude Sonnet 5 accepts text, images, and files such as PDFs as input and returns text."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Which providers serve Claude Sonnet 5?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Claude Sonnet 5 is served by 5 providers on OpenRouter: Claude Platform on AWS, Azure, Google Vertex, Amazon Bedrock, and Anthropic. Requests are routed to the best available provider, with automatic failover to the others, and you can pin or exclude providers with provider routing."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"When was Claude Sonnet 5 released?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Claude Sonnet 5 was released on June 30, 2026."}}]}</script></div><script>$RC("B:9","S:9")</script><div hidden id="S:a"><div class="my-8 w-full first:mt-0"><div class="min-w-0 w-full"><h2>More models from<!-- --> <span class=""><a class="text-inherit underline" href="/anthropic">Anthropic</a></span></h2><div class="mt-4"><div class="overflow-hidden"><section class="group/carousel hover:cursor-move relative w-full" aria-roledescription="carousel"><div><div class="flex -ml-4"><div role="group" aria-roledescription="slide" class="min-w-0 shrink-0 grow-0 pl-4 basis-auto"><a class="group flex h-full w-64 shrink-0 flex-col justify-between gap-y-2 rounded-lg border px-4 py-3 text-left md:w-80" href="/anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5"><div class="line-clamp-1 text-heading font-semibold text-foreground group-hover:text-accent-foreground group-hover:underline">Claude Sonnet 5.5</div><div class="line-clamp-2 text-xs text-muted-foreground"><p class="mb-3 whitespace-pre-wrap break-words leading-6 last:mb-0">Claude Sonnet 5.5 is Anthropic&#x27;s Sonnet-class model for well-scoped everyday work, succeeding Claude Sonnet 5 as a direct upgrade. It is especially strong at building features, fixing bugs, and producing polished documents, slides, and spreadsheets, and it writes and communicates more clearly than its predecessor.</p>
<p class="mb-3 whitespace-pre-wrap break-words leading-6 last:mb-0">Thinking is always on, so effort is the main lever for trading off depth, latency, and cost, and lower effort settings keep it responsive for everyday agentic loops.</p></div><div aria-label="Model details" class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2 gap-y-1 text-overline text-muted-foreground tabular-nums"><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2"><span>Text</span></span><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2"><span aria-hidden="true" class="inline-block size-[0.215em] shrink-0 rounded-full bg-current align-middle"></span><span>1M context</span></span><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2"><span aria-hidden="true" class="inline-block size-[0.215em] shrink-0 rounded-full bg-current align-middle"></span><span>$2 / $10</span></span></div></a></div><div role="group" aria-roledescription="slide" class="min-w-0 shrink-0 grow-0 pl-4 basis-auto"><a class="group flex h-full w-64 shrink-0 flex-col justify-between gap-y-2 rounded-lg border px-4 py-3 text-left md:w-80" href="/anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5:batch"><div class="line-clamp-1 text-heading font-semibold text-foreground group-hover:text-accent-foreground group-hover:underline">Claude Sonnet 5.5</div><div class="line-clamp-2 text-xs text-muted-foreground"><p class="mb-3 whitespace-pre-wrap break-words leading-6 last:mb-0">Claude Sonnet 5.5 is Anthropic&#x27;s Sonnet-class model for well-scoped everyday work, succeeding Claude Sonnet 5 as a direct upgrade. It is especially strong at building features, fixing bugs, and producing polished documents, slides, and spreadsheets, and it writes and communicates more clearly than its predecessor.</p>
<p class="mb-3 whitespace-pre-wrap break-words leading-6 last:mb-0">Thinking is always on, so effort is the main lever for trading off depth, latency, and cost, and lower effort settings keep it responsive for everyday agentic loops.</p></div><div aria-label="Model details" class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2 gap-y-1 text-overline text-muted-foreground tabular-nums"><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2"><span>Text</span></span><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2"><span aria-hidden="true" class="inline-block size-[0.215em] shrink-0 rounded-full bg-current align-middle"></span><span>1M context</span></span><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2"><span aria-hidden="true" class="inline-block size-[0.215em] shrink-0 rounded-full bg-current align-middle"></span><span>$1 / $5</span></span></div></a></div><div role="group" aria-roledescription="slide" class="min-w-0 shrink-0 grow-0 pl-4 basis-auto"><a class="group flex h-full w-64 shrink-0 flex-col justify-between gap-y-2 rounded-lg border px-4 py-3 text-left md:w-80" href="/anthropic/claude-opus-5.5"><div class="line-clamp-1 text-heading font-semibold text-foreground group-hover:text-accent-foreground group-hover:underline">Claude Opus 5.5</div><div class="line-clamp-2 text-xs text-muted-foreground"><p class="mb-3 whitespace-pre-wrap break-words leading-6 last:mb-0">Claude Opus 5.5 is Anthropic&#x27;s flagship model for demanding reasoning, coding, and long-horizon agentic work, succeeding Claude Opus 5. It is particularly strong at multi-step changes in large codebases, code review and bug finding, financial and scientific analysis, and reading dense charts, diagrams, and screenshots, and it is more careful than its predecessor about only stating figures and citing sources it can back up.</p>
<p class="mb-3 whitespace-pre-wrap break-words leading-6 last:mb-0">The model completes comparable tasks in fewer steps and with fewer tokens than Opus 5, and reports on its work in plainer language, with clear updates on what it did, what it found, and what it needs from the user. Thinking is always adaptive, so effort is the main lever for trading off depth, latency, and cost, and lower effort settings remain effective for latency-sensitive workloads.</p></div><div aria-label="Model details" class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2 gap-y-1 text-overline text-muted-foreground tabular-nums"><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2"><span>Text</span></span><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2"><span aria-hidden="true" class="inline-block size-[0.215em] shrink-0 rounded-full bg-current align-middle"></span><span>1M context</span></span><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2"><span aria-hidden="true" class="inline-block size-[0.215em] shrink-0 rounded-full bg-current align-middle"></span><span>$4 / $20</span></span></div></a></div><div role="group" aria-roledescription="slide" class="min-w-0 shrink-0 grow-0 pl-4 basis-auto"><a class="group flex h-full w-64 shrink-0 flex-col justify-between gap-y-2 rounded-lg border px-4 py-3 text-left md:w-80" href="/anthropic/claude-opus-5.5:batch"><div class="line-clamp-1 text-heading font-semibold text-foreground group-hover:text-accent-foreground group-hover:underline">Claude Opus 5.5</div><div class="line-clamp-2 text-xs text-muted-foreground"><p class="mb-3 whitespace-pre-wrap break-words leading-6 last:mb-0">Claude Opus 5.5 is Anthropic&#x27;s flagship model for demanding reasoning, coding, and long-horizon agentic work, succeeding Claude Opus 5. It is particularly strong at multi-step changes in large codebases, code review and bug finding, financial and scientific analysis, and reading dense charts, diagrams, and screenshots, and it is more careful than its predecessor about only stating figures and citing sources it can back up.</p>
<p class="mb-3 whitespace-pre-wrap break-words leading-6 last:mb-0">The model completes comparable tasks in fewer steps and with fewer tokens than Opus 5, and reports on its work in plainer language, with clear updates on what it did, what it found, and what it needs from the user. Thinking is always adaptive, so effort is the main lever for trading off depth, latency, and cost, and lower effort settings remain effective for latency-sensitive workloads.</p></div><div aria-label="Model details" class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2 gap-y-1 text-overline text-muted-foreground tabular-nums"><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2"><span>Text</span></span><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2"><span aria-hidden="true" class="inline-block size-[0.215em] shrink-0 rounded-full bg-current align-middle"></span><span>1M context</span></span><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2"><span aria-hidden="true" class="inline-block size-[0.215em] shrink-0 rounded-full bg-current align-middle"></span><span>$2 / $10</span></span></div></a></div><div role="group" aria-roledescription="slide" class="min-w-0 shrink-0 grow-0 pl-4 basis-auto"><a class="group flex h-full w-64 shrink-0 flex-col justify-between gap-y-2 rounded-lg border px-4 py-3 text-left md:w-80" href="/anthropic/claude-fable-5.1"><div class="line-clamp-1 text-heading font-semibold text-foreground group-hover:text-accent-foreground group-hover:underline">Claude Fable 5.1</div><div class="line-clamp-2 text-xs text-muted-foreground"><p class="mb-3 whitespace-pre-wrap break-words leading-6 last:mb-0">Claude Fable 5.1 improves on Claude Fable 5 across the board, with the biggest gains in agentic coding, long-running agentic workflows, and knowledge work: long code refactors, front-end and visual code generation, and finance and analysis tasks in particular. It also tends to be more concise than Fable 5 in its plans and summaries. We recommend testing it as a direct upgrade wherever you use Fable 5 today, and alongside Opus 5 on reasoning-heavy tasks.</p></div><div aria-label="Model details" class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2 gap-y-1 text-overline text-muted-foreground tabular-nums"><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2"><span>Text</span></span><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2"><span aria-hidden="true" class="inline-block size-[0.215em] shrink-0 rounded-full bg-current align-middle"></span><span>1M context</span></span><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2"><span aria-hidden="true" class="inline-block size-[0.215em] shrink-0 rounded-full bg-current align-middle"></span><span>$10 / $50</span></span></div></a></div><div role="group" aria-roledescription="slide" class="min-w-0 shrink-0 grow-0 pl-4 basis-auto"><a class="group flex h-full w-64 shrink-0 flex-col justify-between gap-y-2 rounded-lg border px-4 py-3 text-left md:w-80" href="/anthropic/claude-fable-5.1:batch"><div class="line-clamp-1 text-heading font-semibold text-foreground group-hover:text-accent-foreground group-hover:underline">Claude Fable 5.1</div><div class="line-clamp-2 text-xs text-muted-foreground"><p class="mb-3 whitespace-pre-wrap break-words leading-6 last:mb-0">Claude Fable 5.1 improves on Claude Fable 5 across the board, with the biggest gains in agentic coding, long-running agentic workflows, and knowledge work: long code refactors, front-end and visual code generation, and finance and analysis tasks in particular. It also tends to be more concise than Fable 5 in its plans and summaries. We recommend testing it as a direct upgrade wherever you use Fable 5 today, and alongside Opus 5 on reasoning-heavy tasks.</p></div><div aria-label="Model details" class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2 gap-y-1 text-overline text-muted-foreground tabular-nums"><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2"><span>Text</span></span><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2"><span aria-hidden="true" class="inline-block size-[0.215em] shrink-0 rounded-full bg-current align-middle"></span><span>1M context</span></span><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2"><span aria-hidden="true" class="inline-block size-[0.215em] shrink-0 rounded-full bg-current align-middle"></span><span>$5 / $25</span></span></div></a></div><div role="group" aria-roledescription="slide" class="min-w-0 shrink-0 grow-0 pl-4 basis-auto"><a class="group flex h-full w-64 shrink-0 flex-col justify-between gap-y-2 rounded-lg border px-4 py-3 text-left md:w-80" href="/anthropic/claude-opus-5-fast"><div class="line-clamp-1 text-heading font-semibold text-foreground group-hover:text-accent-foreground group-hover:underline">Claude Opus 5</div><div class="line-clamp-2 text-xs text-muted-foreground"><p class="mb-3 whitespace-pre-wrap break-words leading-6 last:mb-0">Fast-mode variant of <span>Opus 5</span> - identical capabilities with higher output speed at 2x pricing relative to regular Opus 5.</p>
<p class="mb-3 whitespace-pre-wrap break-words leading-6 last:mb-0">Learn more in Anthropic&#x27;s docs: <span>https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/fast-mode</span></p>
<p class="mb-3 whitespace-pre-wrap break-words leading-6 last:mb-0">Note: As of September 1, 2026, this dedicated fast model is deprecated. Fast mode is now served by the <code class="rounded-md bg-card-hover px-1.5 text-foreground">fast</code> service tier endpoint on <span>Claude Opus 5</span> — request it with <code class="rounded-md bg-card-hover px-1.5 text-foreground">service_tier: &quot;fast&quot;</code> or <code class="rounded-md bg-card-hover px-1.5 text-foreground">speed: &quot;fast&quot;</code>. Requests to this model keep working and are served by the same fast tier capacity, so no action is required, but new integrations should target the regular model. Learn more in our service tier docs: <span>https://openrouter.ai/docs/guides/features/service-tiers</span></p></div><div aria-label="Model details" class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2 gap-y-1 text-overline text-muted-foreground tabular-nums"><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2"><span>Text</span></span><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2"><span aria-hidden="true" class="inline-block size-[0.215em] shrink-0 rounded-full bg-current align-middle"></span><span>1M context</span></span></div></a></div><div role="group" aria-roledescription="slide" class="min-w-0 shrink-0 grow-0 pl-4 basis-auto"><a class="group flex h-full w-64 shrink-0 flex-col justify-between gap-y-2 rounded-lg border px-4 py-3 text-left md:w-80" href="/anthropic/claude-opus-5"><div class="line-clamp-1 text-heading font-semibold text-foreground group-hover:text-accent-foreground group-hover:underline">Claude Opus 5</div><div class="line-clamp-2 text-xs text-muted-foreground"><p class="mb-3 whitespace-pre-wrap break-words leading-6 last:mb-0">Claude Opus 5 is Anthropic’s flagship model for demanding reasoning, coding, and long-horizon agentic work. It is particularly strong at end-to-end software tasks, code review and bug finding, visual analysis of charts and documents, complex office deliverables, and coordinating parallel subagents.</p>
<p class="mb-3 whitespace-pre-wrap break-words leading-6 last:mb-0">The model maintains strong instruction following and tool use across extended tasks, while remaining effective at lower effort settings for workloads that prioritize latency and token efficiency.</p></div><div aria-label="Model details" class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2 gap-y-1 text-overline text-muted-foreground tabular-nums"><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2"><span>Text</span></span><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2"><span aria-hidden="true" class="inline-block size-[0.215em] shrink-0 rounded-full bg-current align-middle"></span><span>1M context</span></span><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2"><span aria-hidden="true" class="inline-block size-[0.215em] shrink-0 rounded-full bg-current align-middle"></span><span>$5 / $25</span></span></div></a></div><div role="group" aria-roledescription="slide" class="min-w-0 shrink-0 grow-0 pl-4 basis-auto"><a class="group flex h-full w-64 shrink-0 flex-col justify-between gap-y-2 rounded-lg border px-4 py-3 text-left md:w-80" href="/anthropic/claude-opus-5:batch"><div class="line-clamp-1 text-heading font-semibold text-foreground group-hover:text-accent-foreground group-hover:underline">Claude Opus 5</div><div class="line-clamp-2 text-xs text-muted-foreground"><p class="mb-3 whitespace-pre-wrap break-words leading-6 last:mb-0">Claude Opus 5 is Anthropic’s flagship model for demanding reasoning, coding, and long-horizon agentic work. It is particularly strong at end-to-end software tasks, code review and bug finding, visual analysis of charts and documents, complex office deliverables, and coordinating parallel subagents.</p>
<p class="mb-3 whitespace-pre-wrap break-words leading-6 last:mb-0">The model maintains strong instruction following and tool use across extended tasks, while remaining effective at lower effort settings for workloads that prioritize latency and token efficiency.</p></div><div aria-label="Model details" class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2 gap-y-1 text-overline text-muted-foreground tabular-nums"><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2"><span>Text</span></span><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2"><span aria-hidden="true" class="inline-block size-[0.215em] shrink-0 rounded-full bg-current align-middle"></span><span>1M context</span></span><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2"><span aria-hidden="true" class="inline-block size-[0.215em] shrink-0 rounded-full bg-current align-middle"></span><span>$2.50 / $12.50</span></span></div></a></div><div role="group" aria-roledescription="slide" class="min-w-0 shrink-0 grow-0 pl-4 basis-auto"><a class="group flex h-full w-64 shrink-0 flex-col justify-between gap-y-2 rounded-lg border px-4 py-3 text-left md:w-80" href="/anthropic/claude-sonnet-5:batch"><div class="line-clamp-1 text-heading font-semibold text-foreground group-hover:text-accent-foreground group-hover:underline">Claude Sonnet 5</div><div class="line-clamp-2 text-xs text-muted-foreground"><p class="mb-3 whitespace-pre-wrap break-words leading-6 last:mb-0">Sonnet 5 is Anthropic&#x27;s most capable Sonnet-class model, with frontier performance across coding, agents, and professional work. It supports adaptive thinking with selectable reasoning effort levels (low, medium, high, max, and x-high), a 1M-token context window, and text, image, and file inputs. Sonnet 5 uses an updated tokenizer and includes real-time cyber safeguards that block certain high-risk dual-use activities.</p></div><div aria-label="Model details" class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2 gap-y-1 text-overline text-muted-foreground tabular-nums"><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2"><span>Text</span></span><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2"><span aria-hidden="true" class="inline-block size-[0.215em] shrink-0 rounded-full bg-current align-middle"></span><span>1M context</span></span><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2"><span aria-hidden="true" class="inline-block size-[0.215em] shrink-0 rounded-full bg-current align-middle"></span><span>$1 / $5</span></span></div></a></div><div role="group" aria-roledescription="slide" class="min-w-0 shrink-0 grow-0 pl-4 basis-auto"><a class="group flex h-full w-64 shrink-0 flex-col justify-between gap-y-2 rounded-lg border px-4 py-3 text-left md:w-80" href="/~anthropic/claude-fable-latest"><div class="line-clamp-1 text-heading font-semibold text-foreground group-hover:text-accent-foreground group-hover:underline">Claude Fable Latest</div><div class="line-clamp-2 text-xs text-muted-foreground"><p class="mb-3 whitespace-pre-wrap break-words leading-6 last:mb-0">This model always redirects to the latest model in the Claude Fable family.</p></div><div aria-label="Model details" class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2 gap-y-1 text-overline text-muted-foreground tabular-nums"><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2"><span>Text</span></span><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2"><span aria-hidden="true" class="inline-block size-[0.215em] shrink-0 rounded-full bg-current align-middle"></span><span>1M context</span></span></div></a></div><div role="group" aria-roledescription="slide" class="min-w-0 shrink-0 grow-0 pl-4 basis-auto"><a class="group flex h-full w-64 shrink-0 flex-col justify-between gap-y-2 rounded-lg border px-4 py-3 text-left md:w-80" href="/anthropic/claude-fable-5"><div class="line-clamp-1 text-heading font-semibold text-foreground group-hover:text-accent-foreground group-hover:underline">Claude Fable 5</div><div class="line-clamp-2 text-xs text-muted-foreground"><p class="mb-3 whitespace-pre-wrap break-words leading-6 last:mb-0">Claude Fable 5 is a Mythos-class model from Anthropic, built for autonomous knowledge work and coding. It supports text, image, and file inputs with text output, with reasoning support and a 1M-token context window. It is suited for long-running, complex, and asynchronous tasks that previously required frequent human check-ins.</p>
<p class="mb-3 whitespace-pre-wrap break-words leading-6 last:mb-0">It is particularly strong at end-to-end work that would otherwise take a person hours, days, or weeks - taking on problems that are long-running, ambiguous, or highly multi-step. It executes well-scoped tasks with few mistakes, automatically self-correcting through verification loops, and ships with robust safeguards.</p></div><div aria-label="Model details" class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2 gap-y-1 text-overline text-muted-foreground tabular-nums"><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2"><span>Text</span></span><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2"><span aria-hidden="true" class="inline-block size-[0.215em] shrink-0 rounded-full bg-current align-middle"></span><span>1M context</span></span><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2"><span aria-hidden="true" class="inline-block size-[0.215em] shrink-0 rounded-full bg-current align-middle"></span><span>$10 / $50</span></span></div></a></div><div role="group" aria-roledescription="slide" class="min-w-0 shrink-0 grow-0 pl-4 basis-auto"><a class="group flex h-full w-64 shrink-0 flex-col justify-between gap-y-2 rounded-lg border px-4 py-3 text-left md:w-80" href="/anthropic/claude-fable-5:batch"><div class="line-clamp-1 text-heading font-semibold text-foreground group-hover:text-accent-foreground group-hover:underline">Claude Fable 5</div><div class="line-clamp-2 text-xs text-muted-foreground"><p class="mb-3 whitespace-pre-wrap break-words leading-6 last:mb-0">Claude Fable 5 is a Mythos-class model from Anthropic, built for autonomous knowledge work and coding. It supports text, image, and file inputs with text output, with reasoning support and a 1M-token context window. It is suited for long-running, complex, and asynchronous tasks that previously required frequent human check-ins.</p>
<p class="mb-3 whitespace-pre-wrap break-words leading-6 last:mb-0">It is particularly strong at end-to-end work that would otherwise take a person hours, days, or weeks - taking on problems that are long-running, ambiguous, or highly multi-step. It executes well-scoped tasks with few mistakes, automatically self-correcting through verification loops, and ships with robust safeguards.</p></div><div aria-label="Model details" class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2 gap-y-1 text-overline text-muted-foreground tabular-nums"><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2"><span>Text</span></span><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2"><span aria-hidden="true" class="inline-block size-[0.215em] shrink-0 rounded-full bg-current align-middle"></span><span>1M context</span></span><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2"><span aria-hidden="true" class="inline-block size-[0.215em] shrink-0 rounded-full bg-current align-middle"></span><span>$5 / $25</span></span></div></a></div><div role="group" aria-roledescription="slide" class="min-w-0 shrink-0 grow-0 pl-4 basis-auto"><a class="group flex h-full w-64 shrink-0 flex-col justify-between gap-y-2 rounded-lg border px-4 py-3 text-left md:w-80" href="/anthropic/claude-opus-4.8-fast"><div class="line-clamp-1 text-heading font-semibold text-foreground group-hover:text-accent-foreground group-hover:underline">Claude Opus 4.8</div><div class="line-clamp-2 text-xs text-muted-foreground"><p class="mb-3 whitespace-pre-wrap break-words leading-6 last:mb-0">Fast-mode variant of <span>Opus 4.8</span> - identical capabilities with higher output speed at 2x pricing relative to regular Opus 4.8.</p>
